  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Glycyrrhizic acid, the sweet-tasting main constituent of liquorice, is a liver therapy drug used for liver conditions. It is an approved medicine, though its use appears limited and it is also being studied investigationally; it is not an EMA-authorised product.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q418705&quot;>Wikidata Q418705</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>glycyrrhizic acid</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>A05BA08</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB13751&quot;>DB13751</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/14982&quot;>14982</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:15939&quot;>15939</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q418705&quot;>Q418705</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C42H62O16</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>822.942 g/mol (PubChem)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
